{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/928210-weird-npcs-jusr-fo-fun","id":928210,"title":"Weird NPCs [Jusr Fo Fun]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-08T09:32:34-07:00","id":928210,"title":"Weird NPCs [Jusr Fo Fun]","content":"last night, I've had a dream that Onyx Path has made a new supplement called &quot;Weird NPCs&quot;- which was a detailed book filled with many strange, ready made characters for the game (well, that and something called &quot;angels&quot;- porcelain like beings who snitch people through shadows). Anyway, I didn't had a lot of time to read the book because of those &quot;angels&quot;, but I did managed to read about one character- Jormo Bromo, a strix which used synthesis on a werewolf and became a time traveler. through some God Machine mechanism. That made me thought that maybe such supplement for weird NPCs who look like a mish mash of many of the setting's elements could be a cool thing to tinker with. So- does anyone has ideas for other Weird NPCs or how to state Jormo the time travelling strix?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:29:03-07:00","id":928298,"title":"","content":"More of a weird NPC I enjoy, the wonky fortuneteller. They might be an oracle in the ancient tradition, or someone who sees signs of the future in the most obscure of things. Either way, they're only half right. Most of the times less. But for what they are right about, they're spot on. Basically they spin circuitous divinations of future events for the players, but only one part is correct. A cell of hunters might be told that they're going to investigate a recent death and encounter a vampire and their minions, so should bring a silver blade to pierce its heart and end it. However, after hearing about a recent death and going through the investigation they find out it was a demiurge who was collecting body parts to make their Promethean. On the way back from the mad scientist's lair they get accosted by a vicious werewolf, for which they will need a silver weapon. I've found it works better as a recurring character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T18:49:10-07:00","id":928549,"title":"","content":"The current lead antagonist in my game is a Changeling who's keeper is the caretaker of the Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn (in my game both Arcadias are the same). When he escaped his Durance, he didn't leave Arcadia by the Hedge, he left through the Abyss.<br /> <br /> For less blatantly rule breaking mixes, in the local goblin market is a dark stall, filled with death touched items. A Sin Eater will quickly identify these items as Mementos. The stall is kept by an animate shadow called Madame Mortality. In actuality, she is an unbound Geist who has managed to find her way to the Hedge, and acquired a market stall. Rumor is, if you bring her a fresh corpse, she'll trade it for a death mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T03:38:01-07:00","id":928671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/928210-weird-npcs-jusr-fo-fun?p=928549#post928549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For less blatantly rule breaking mixes, in the local goblin market is a dark stall, filled with death touched items. A Sin Eater will quickly identify these items as Mementos. The stall is kept by an animate shadow called Madame Mortality. In actuality, she is an unbound Geist who has managed to find her way to the Hedge, and acquired a market stall. Rumor is, if you bring her a fresh corpse, she'll trade it for a death mask.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this one. It perfectly encapsulates Changeling's taste for the odd, and Geist's &quot;Why Not?&quot; feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:03:20-07:00","id":928751,"title":"","content":"Remember the shoe shine from Police Squad? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7udsYPVhl6Y\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7udsYPVhl6Y</a> ?<br /> I've had a NPC in my Mage game who only appeared at night in a back alley, doing the shoe shining for token cash prize. He was stressed, disturbing and usually very quiet, but if you asked him something - or just pushed him to talk - he would flood you with under-breath, pretty creepy comments about your past, future, present and fate, with a tell tale signs of supernal insight he didn't understand or comprehend. He talked very quickly, and when displaying his magical insight, he would end his sentences with &quot;but what do I know, I'm just a shoe shine&quot;, which should sound funny, but in the context of his scenes was pretty creepy.<br /> <br /> During day, dude was a normal guy with normal family, and would remember going to bed and just having a recurring dream about shoe shining in the back alley. Mages left him alone, scared of interfering with potential Awakening (that nobody could track, because noone knew how long he was around), and while he was harmless, somehow nobody tried to hurt him. Sometimes, people would go to him if they needed advice, or some Time-Fate nudge, and they would always give him a dollar, because without a dollar, you couldn't trigger his oracle-trance.<br /> <br /> He was weird and very surreal, his scenes were full of onirism and detachment from reality, and I'm really glad I tackled this concept, because while it sounded funny on paper, it ended up being really, really disturbing in practice, and nobody laughed. No sir, they didn't laugh.<br /> <br /> His &quot;perk&quot; was ability to read anything Fate and Time related from your shoes, which has some neat and simple symbolism. Enlightened Madness is probably the best word to describe it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-09-2016, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T12:52:51-07:00","id":928873,"title":"","content":"I once had an idea for a hobgoblin psychologist/witch doctor who lived in a spooky mansion filled with remedies for and notes on mental and spiritual ailments of various supernaturals. He was supposed to be a changeling at first, but I eventually settled for hobgoblin. To him, everything goes when trying to fix a serious problem, be it weird goblin vegetable soup to hands-on oneiromancy sessions. He'd be a jack of all trades, focusing on Crafts, Academics, Empathy and Occult. His specialty was in changelings, but he helped other hobgoblins and even ghosts.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about giving him a Fae Aspect that mimics the Skeleton Key of Beasts, and another that helps with recovering the Integrity traits or Conditions of his patients.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}